    "terrainName": "basic-desert",
    "description": "What: Temperament & Stress \u00a76 (CE-2271, R-2034/R-2075) - two mirrored duels on open basic-desert, 300 m apart: 'Bold' (Friend rifleman, bravery 0.9) at (200,300) and 'Cautious' (Friend rifleman, bravery 0.1), both obedience 0.3 so character shows, each ordered to attack (CombatPosture, advance to 5 m short of his enemy) 'Bold Enemy' / 'Cautious Enemy' (Hostile riflemen holding a spot behind a car 100 m north, InertSop); a car 8 m in front of each attacker is his nearest cover. All immortal. Judge (90 s): (1) the bold man's posture is AdvanceAndAttack for more of the time than the cautious man's; (2) the cautious man takes cover or suppresses for more of the time than the bold man; (3) the bold man ends nearer his enemy; (4) printed: each man's posture time shares and the damping modifiers in his utility trace. Check: python3 scripts/utility-demo-check.py --launch ts-aggression. \ud83d\udcc4 docs/DESIGN_Temperament_And_Stress.md \u00a76"
  },
